#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228910 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5bc609b-dc5b-52e9-9f0e-206f32bb829b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Homogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/id #uuid "26df399d-cd87-5b5d-9f3f-7ced4ca5fd06" :question/math-academy-id "e-21707" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-7x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-7y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to the system of ODEs above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/4c/4c7ca8aa3fb83e7c4ce806080257e8f3b3d5186e19f10649a0bed7202f6501b6.svg) where ![](images/04/0492dd33f8d39d4a74139be25415d6d943888d8ccbf67158690f0960c5334415.svg)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/85/85304407fca2ace2d7fb5d97123e1f27f45386c8f3ebcc1a1c3859d1b573d2b0.svg)\nwhere ![](images/81/81bcc770826e2156f310569f014356cc686541259c11aa190ac28394a6d38725.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/31/310669815cad029379ffa4022fa9094ef8597d91496c57f70c66ed51926836b3.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system is given by\n![](images/e1/e128d7d4610a3a9021b1391f278822bcdf113570500b822c05370e473923f5b7.svg)\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-7t} & t{e}^{-7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-7t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-7t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-7t} \\\\ {e}^{-7t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-7t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-7t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228911 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229145 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems"}] :question/id #uuid "ace067cd-e1d0-5b3e-bae2-bf58dcac3585" :question/math-academy-id "e-21711" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\Phi_0'(t) = A\\Phi_0(t), \\qquad \\Phi_0(0) = I_n.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ passing through $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\textrm{L1}{:}\\;$ Let $\\Phi_0(t)=e^{At}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L2}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\Phi_0(t)\\,\\mathbf{c}$ for some constant vector $\\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L3}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{At}\\,\\mathbf{c}$ \n\n$\\textrm{L4}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L5}{:}\\;$ $(e^{A t_0})^{-1} \\mathbf{x}(t_0)=(e^{At_0})^{-1} e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L6}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{c} = e^{-A t_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L7}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At} e^{-At_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L8}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At - At_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L9}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{A(t-t_0)} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\nFill in the blanks to justify each step of the following reasoning.\n\n$\\qquad$ Line $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from $\\textrm{L4}$ by ![](images/b2/b2df506469d945a843b7784f38a1b12d6f89016aee1fb12581705b6d9d98baab.svg)\n\n$\\qquad$ The property of the matrix exponential used in $\\textrm{L8}$ is ![](images/7a/7af985a90d901c63f7d03feda679d513fa18ccb36d34c8fb237ac755baf9f801.svg)\n\n$\\qquad$ Line $\\textrm{L9}$ follows from $\\textrm{L8}$ by the fact that  ![](images/c5/c55c24e30a71bf93cdd21c2a5d0f3c68271cd6fb3f2033b84ce8338569eacd4a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\textrm{L4}$ and $\\textrm{L5}.$ Starting from $\\textrm{L4},$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwe multiply both sides on the left by $(e^{At_0})^{-1}$ to get\n\n$$\n(e^{A t_0})^{-1}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=(e^{At_0})^{-1}e^{A t_0}\\,\\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\textrm{L5}.$ Therefore, $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from $\\textrm{L4}$ by ![](images/22/2226897d3c49c80358dc93ec1d1d80bd8b513764e6b39bbf93408215c83144bf.svg)\n\n- Next, we justify the step $\\textrm{L7}$ to $\\textrm{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-At_0$ commute, we may combine exponentials:\n\n$$\ne^{At}e^{-At_0}=e^{At-At_0}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\textrm{L7}$ produces line $\\textrm{L8}.$ Hence, the property of the matrix exponential used in $\\textrm{L8}$ is ![](images/e4/e4a1c6f6b74ea7491973a3bfa76225f1f6af67a681582a49afa51772c05bfaed.svg)\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\textrm{L8}$ and $\\textrm{L9}.$ Starting from $\\textrm{L8},$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{At-At_0}\\mathbf{x}(t_0),\n$$\n\nwe rewrite the exponent using the algebraic identity $At-At_0=A(t-t_0)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\textrm{L9}.$ Thus, $\\textrm{L9}$ follows from $\\textrm{L8}$ by the fact that $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt lightgray]{At-At_0=A(t-t_0)\\text{ for any }t\\text{ and }t_0}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228917 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/id #uuid "b061f2b1-b015-582f-921f-9b444db631ee" :question/math-academy-id "e-21723" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0d7ecb854b93b475f1897f7ae66e0e459a5ad22247a9d9a5c11adff32b747e4.svg)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/50/50c3d207258cc321a19532b7b54da568a4a6361dde55f35247fe60e931fe5f93.svg) where ![](images/59/599d579a41d84635ae3a34867759b69af6b406d433c4c11a53898f69e856371e.svg)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/6d/6dfab7c1edb51450a9238b3fd1154c7d4a5dccb47c689c54768c4b6cc952c068.svg)\nwhere ![](images/eb/eb99201c10627a06594c4967ac8f3a56cb75784f1f824332a9b58a10aaf672bc.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/e7/e70ec908edd1985f4f1f719dceee192536c0bcdf0b4deedcf1c9f785005ee041.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\mathbf{c} =e^{At} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t = t_0,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0) = e^{At_0} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nand since $e^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c} = e^{-At_0} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $\\mathbf{x}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228918 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/id #uuid "ead811e0-8551-5b15-8b49-711cbe0b8498" :question/math-academy-id "e-21725" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6e456b14ca5110a5cf290cd0053bd52652c8d44e2e9f517f73d2b257c355b8cf.svg)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/e4/e43485cd9eaca81dd04089924a83a909594e575d76d195850cf11719809acbbd.svg) where ![](images/6a/6ac1e35cee6cfbab9771278c3a68f422e5422ef79e4f516755e35748ea402e08.svg)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/b4/b434d5c8a601c3d7fae734a5b78437457fab7877fe0ca1ff466197817d9d1c0e.svg)\nwhere ![](images/cc/cc9313ae17390c751e51673c53d788c24308f501fa7107e3098cd370028eb1d2.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/1d/1d3df45727a13bfbc41ab2689fd1a9a6dbcc28fd4ed071a430a2e745e99aeec8.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\, \\mathbf{x}(0),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{x}(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n![](images/a9/a998751dcfc2e8acb4e142c5b4a5241ec61fe3bc087dccf9fe87344d73b04ce3.svg)\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf4d923b-f1e0-5200-b875-952e608fe146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306935} {:answer/id #uuid "5dde915f-8d58-5806-8670-d44aa8a12efa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(2t)+2\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dde915f-8d58-5806-8670-d44aa8a12efa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(2t)+2\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445558} :answer-field/id #uuid "250c7dc4-5bbf-5745-996d-cb98d0a787e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5c2da58-df61-583a-81eb-de777d114871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307429} {:answer/id #uuid "0a087c4f-5999-5d51-b329-5bde4e70b5a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\cos(2t)+2\\sin(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a087c4f-5999-5d51-b329-5bde4e70b5a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\cos(2t)+2\\sin(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445539} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7fc44b4-bb76-5cfd-8ecc-9c61d46d594b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b59372b5-46f1-5738-9ccc-9025ae0786e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-333971" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150px\">\n{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229658 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229145 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddf47bd1-795c-5a11-b0e3-f0b2b9e331e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372649} {:answer/id #uuid "e05d0157-509e-54f8-93bf-caebcef52673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372650} {:answer/id #uuid "53c2eeb0-49da-574f-9fed-3cc20c2d56d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372651} {:answer/id #uuid "5df25e2f-ebee-57ed-9dbd-3fafe0df4480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e05d0157-509e-54f8-93bf-caebcef52673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372650} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab481dec-1ae8-51be-b85b-70941d4f372c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372648} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cd12299-483e-5c98-8cfb-5093a259f798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372654} {:answer/id #uuid "b990c9db-e47d-504f-b7c8-8d1733bf87d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372655} {:answer/id #uuid "9a41c693-9645-5cfb-8568-d811fb43680c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "using diagonalization of $Φ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372656} {:answer/id #uuid "7a791c9f-84b0-50a6-a430-c32ad39fb614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cd12299-483e-5c98-8cfb-5093a259f798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372654} :answer-field/id #uuid "43bc5aa5-c908-54a0-806e-2624e338ba95" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372653} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57ded996-9ccb-5cb5-9fc2-680c811cefe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372659} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e83cb1-0838-5822-8ae9-639267505411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a solution curve" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372660} {:answer/id #uuid "e7646179-3ccc-53ad-8251-b2fa9008ceb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of the determinant" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372661} {:answer/id #uuid "e3fcb9e7-6ca1-51d4-b6b1-6590bd634d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57ded996-9ccb-5cb5-9fc2-680c811cefe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372659} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a65b927-0188-538b-ab8c-226d64585514" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c2234c8-1637-5807-8336-81efdf9ec90b" :question/math-academy-id "q-333992" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$ \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix, every solution of the system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c\\,\\text{for some constant vector }c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Evaluating the identity $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ at $t=0$ gives \n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445610 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5bc609b-dc5b-52e9-9f0e-206f32bb829b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Homogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cade7c7-d983-59b8-9669-6f8e3582aaa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445549} {:answer/id #uuid "613c735f-5122-5927-a809-bc329b4307b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445560} {:answer/id #uuid "8524af80-eac0-5f3d-ba4c-7130ca74bc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445571} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf2a9b4-44d2-5fb1-9e1f-8e147e929ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445580} {:answer/id #uuid "dfd5e439-6415-5c58-b198-adfa34053c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdf2a9b4-44d2-5fb1-9e1f-8e147e929ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445580} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f0167e8-c854-5755-b6be-76017465421b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4daa880b-394e-5da4-a6f8-c7b8b600dc37" :question/math-academy-id "q-334765" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5bc609b-dc5b-52e9-9f0e-206f32bb829b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Homogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "488cb1f7-d8f3-5937-97b2-5b2c3a66bfcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305859} {:answer/id #uuid "7cea238c-07f8-5863-ba42-90a0781222f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306341} {:answer/id #uuid "b848c94a-ae19-555c-95f9-7d283a1b9bd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306871} {:answer/id #uuid "db15f24c-e0ad-5bfa-961c-cf25f1fe35cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307179} {:answer/id #uuid "e34b718c-be14-565b-b4a8-a3219f881b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db15f24c-e0ad-5bfa-961c-cf25f1fe35cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307179} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b95a712-9c8b-5b50-9226-58266ec793db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c150290d-e2c6-53a1-8ef9-89cbb210da93" :question/math-academy-id "q-334766" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=6x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=6y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6t} & t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6t} & t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6t} & t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{6t} \\\\ {e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229142 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5bc609b-dc5b-52e9-9f0e-206f32bb829b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Homogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "224adb82-b3c8-52f2-b2a6-c9f7f9772557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445548} {:answer/id #uuid "78df560a-fa85-549b-b255-86f7ab415d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445564} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc2c6d7-54ef-53d5-a2b9-59e64b6ad531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445565} {:answer/id #uuid "d56c2436-b44b-5b68-adea-27e2397d0ff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445584} {:answer/id #uuid "ec69783d-87bb-509c-94b8-4b2db9acc468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78df560a-fa85-549b-b255-86f7ab415d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445564} :answer-field/id #uuid "d08bec31-d229-5948-b097-4d0df5e00ec6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {